														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847146">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>I find the image of a trans person physically slicing the embodiment of transphobia from themselves to be very powerful, and the final line is basically the closest this thing can have to a happy ending. I'm wondering, do you have any suggestions for making that final paragraph more impactful or obviously important to the metaphor?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The problem here is that making it land better feels like it's&#8230;a lot more likely to feel jarring? Really though, my issue is more that the ending feels&#8230;not climactic enough? And I'm not sure how to make this feel more climactic tbh without leaning more into the darkness. This said: it might just be my natural inclination towards darker writing that's coming through here rather than an objective truth.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I did consider this, but decided against it as really, these aren't parasites as we understand them but are rather the embodiment of the gender that people feel a trans person should have. Therefore, their ultimate purpose is to totally usurp the host like a cuckoo bird, not to propagate.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Like, I get this and accept your reasoning for this but it feels, to me, a little too loose and up in the air without the propagation; but at the end of the day, this is your call.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure how to incorporate it or trim it, although it seems important for thematic purposes that it remain in some form.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It'd work better if there was some additional connection here; where like, -1 is the only one who can affect which way -2 goes but it feels&#8230;too much like that'd be putting everything on one person when really it's everyone that affects stuff. Honestly, I don't think it really adds much and I'd just trim it completely if you're not going to e.g. tie it into the end cycle or something instead.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

