						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13897952/scp-xxxx">SCP-XXXX</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847141">
									

<p>Well basically, by investigating that room and the house that it is in, they discover that years ago, 7 young girls who had a slumber party there were found dead in the room. The police never found out what happened, but the Foundation suspect another potential SCP to have been responsible. When they died, the room was impregnated with the remnants of the girls' souls with the feeling they had when they died. That's how SCP-XXXX was created. Now, whenever someone enters the room, they are &quot;possessed&quot; by the remnants, and act as previously described. The remnents then behave like some kind of virus, spreading from one person to another through a pillow fight. That's why it could potentially cause the end of the world. If everyone starts running around giggling and pillowfighting forever, human civilization would collapse.</p>
<p>As to how to bring it up, I was thinking of having the Foundation investigate and learn about the 7 girls (as previously stated), then do experiences and talking with one of the possessed one. Then they'll understand that this person is possessed with the remnants of the girls' souls though dialogue.</p>
<p>I know it sounds jarring, but that's why I like it. I love SCPs that are seemingly funny or ridiculous, just to be revealed to actually be dangerous and creepy.</p>

							</div>

								
					
